## Writing a new case (for humans)

If you want to log a case manually (no `harness_` prefix), create it as
`cases/<your-slug>.md`. harness will grep-match it but never edit it.

Minimum threshold (for harness auto-collection): case must meet at least 2 of:
- Diagnosis took over 30 minutes
- Crossed module boundaries
- Recurred at least once
- Platform / browser / provider-specific
- Visible to end users or production
- Invalidated a prior assumption

## Reading cases (for agents)

Before editing code under `src/`, grep this file + `cases/*.md` by:
- Changed file path and module name
- Exported symbols you're about to modify
- Error messages from stack traces
- Browser / dependency names

Match types: `applies_to.paths` glob = strong; two weak signals = weak.
Output a `Memory check:` line in your response citing matches.
